-- title:
--   Wild automorphisms act with p-power order on finite normal levels
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be a field extension, let $p$ be a prime number, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $L$ satisfying `LiesOverPrime p`, that is, the image of $p$ in $L$ lies in the set of nonunits of $P$. Let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ which is wild at $P$ in the sense that for every nonzero $z \in L$ the element $\sigma(z) \cdot z^{-1} - 1$ is a nonunit of $P$. Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $L/K$ which is finite-dimensional over $K$ and normal over $K$. The conclusion is that there exists a natural number $a$ such that $\sigma^{p^{a}}$ fixes $F$ pointwise: $(\sigma^{p^{a}})(x) = x$ for every $x \in F$. No discreteness, completeness or Noetherian hypothesis on $P$ is imposed, and $K$ is an arbitrary base field; the exponent $a$ is produced by the proof and is not otherwise constrained.
--
--   This is the base-free form of the classical fact that the wild inertia (first ramification) group of a valued extension is a pro-$p$ group, $p$ being the residue characteristic: the closed subgroup generated by a wild automorphism has $p$-power image at every finite normal level. It feeds into the construction of Frobenius elements with prescribed wild behaviour at a discrete valuation, used in [`ValuationSubring.exists_isFrobeniusAt_pow_forall_inertiaSubgroupIn_conj_mul_pow_inv_wild_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_isFrobeniusAt_pow_forall_inertiaSubgroupIn_conj_mul_pow_inv_wild_of_isDiscreteValuationRing).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_forall_pow_prime_pow_apply_eq_of_wild_of_normal.lean

